# Productivity Board

A personal Kanban-style productivity tracker for planning days, weeks and months.
Built with vanilla JavaScript on the front end and Flask + SQLite on the back end.

![Board view](127.0.0.1_5000_.png.png)

## Features

- Kanban board with To Do, In Progress and Completed columns
- Add, edit, delete and move tasks (colors follow the column)
- Reminders at a fixed interval once a task is started
- End-of-day review: see what is still open, move tasks to tomorrow, write a reflection
- Notes panel with categories (habit, reflection, time management, critique, other)
- Day, week and month planner views based on due dates
- Light, dark and system themes

## Tech stack

- **Front end:** HTML, CSS, vanilla JavaScript (ES modules)
- **Back end:** Python, Flask, SQLite
- **API:** REST endpoints for tasks (`/api/tasks`) and notes (`/api/notes`)

## Run it locally

```
git clone https://github.com/azizshahid/Kaban-board.git
cd Kaban-board
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate        # Windows (macOS/Linux: source venv/bin/activate)
pip install flask
python backend/app.py
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:5000/

The database (`backend/board.db`) is created automatically on first run and is
not committed to Git.

## Project structure

```
frontend/   index.html, index.js, storage.js, style.css, panels.css, planner.css, theme.css
backend/    app.py
```

## Notes

- Reminders only fire while the page is open in a browser tab.
- Theme and reminder interval are stored per device in `localStorage`; tasks and notes live in SQLite.